WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:12.890
Do you have anything in your home that you never use but can't bear to throw out? Maybe

2
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:18.370
some old toys from your childhood, or books that you never finished reading, or an outdated

3
00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:24.130
cell phone that you think you might need in an emergency. Everyone hangs on to some items

4
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:30.330
longer than is necessary, but hoarders take this practice to the extreme.

5
00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:36.210
Hoarding is a form of behavior which means that a person simply cannot part with anything.

6
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:41.490
It is more than just the desire to collect old things. Hoarders hold on to everything

7
00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:47.370
they own forever, no matter how useless it may seem to others. Commonly hoarded items

8
00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:53.210
include personal possessions like clothes and photographs, as well as more unusual things

9
00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:59.090
such as buttons and old electronics. Some people even keep garbage like old newspapers

10
00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:06.410
and advertisements. One woman reported needing 58 enormous boxes to carry useless art supplies

11
00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:12.370
with her when she moved to a new house. But hoarding isn't just an unusual personal

12
00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:18.530
characteristic. It can lead to serious consequences for people. For one thing, hoarders tend to

13
00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:24.490
be very disorganized. Boxes and rooms fill up with trash, and this can lead to a dirty

14
00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:30.530
and unhealthy living situation. Another problem is the emotional impact on the hoarder's

15
00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:36.210
family. Imagine living with a family member who gets upset any time you try to throw something

16
00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:44.090
away. It can be incredibly stressful for everyone involved. Hoarding is recognized as a psychological

17
00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:49.730
problem, so it is possible for hoarders to get treatment. One woman participated in a

18
00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:55.650
30-day program which encouraged her to throw out one item on the first day, two on the second day,

19
00:01:55.650 --> 00:02:02.890
and so on. Throwing away your trash may seem simple and natural to most of us. For hoarders,

20
00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:09.250
though, it can be a long and often painful road to cleaning up both their homes and their lives.
